d 'WHICHDIDSHOULDIUSE': module to classify a panel's difference-in-differences design
d
d      whichdidshouldiuse reads a panel and classifies its
d difference-in-differences design as CLA, SAD, HAD, SFSD or OTHER,
d names a	 suitable estimator, and points you at the relevant
d chapter of Clement de Chaisemartin and Xavier D'Haultfoeuille's  
d      difference-in-differences textbook.    It classifies; it
d does not estimate. There are no fixed effects, weights or
d standard-error options, because nothing is being	  fitted. 
d
d KW: panel data
d KW: DiD
d KW: TWFE
d
d Requires: Stata version 16 and distinct, did_had, gtools from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261024
d
d Author:   Alberto Trelles,  Sciences Po
d Support: email chaisemartin.packages@@gmail.com
d
d Author: Clement de Chaisemartin,  Sciences Po
d Support: email clementdechaisemartin@@gmail.com
d
d Author:  Anzony Quispe ,  Brown University
d Support: email chaisemartin.packages@@gmail.com
d
f whichdidshouldiuse.ado
f whichdidshouldiuse.sthlp
f ../g/gentzkowetal_didtextbook.dta
f ../m/moser_voena_didtextbook.dta
f ../p/pierce_schott_didtextbook.dta
f wolfers2006_didtextbook.dta
